{"componentChunkName":"component---src-templates-post-js","path":"/posts/streaming-gemini-responses-into-angular-signals/","result":{"data":{"markdownRemark":{"html":"<p><span\n      class=\"gatsby-resp-image-wrapper\"\n      style=\"position: relative; display: block; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto; max-width: 1280px; \"\n    >\n      <a\n    class=\"gatsby-resp-image-link\"\n    href=\"/static/c4cf17fff5f67c64622039a64d9e63ac/00711/hero.png\"\n    style=\"display: block\"\n    target=\"_blank\"\n    rel=\"noopener\"\n  >\n    <span\n    class=\"gatsby-resp-image-background-image\"\n    style=\"padding-bottom: 33.4375%; position: relative; bottom: 0; left: 0; background-image: url('data:image/png;base64,'); background-size: cover; display: block;\"\n  ></span>\n  <picture>\n          <source\n              srcset=\"/static/c4cf17fff5f67c64622039a64d9e63ac/fb34c/hero.avif 320w,\n/static/c4cf17fff5f67c64622039a64d9e63ac/646cd/hero.avif 768w,\n/static/c4cf17fff5f67c64622039a64d9e63ac/8b485/hero.avif 1024w,\n/static/c4cf17fff5f67c64622039a64d9e63ac/a73d6/hero.avif 1280w,\n/static/c4cf17fff5f67c64622039a64d9e63ac/a7f9f/hero.avif 1920w,\n/static/c4cf17fff5f67c64622039a64d9e63ac/fb732/hero.avif 2400w\"\n              sizes=\"(max-width: 1280px) 100vw, 1280px\"\n              type=\"image/avif\"\n            /><source\n              srcset=\"/static/c4cf17fff5f67c64622039a64d9e63ac/cb523/hero.webp 320w,\n/static/c4cf17fff5f67c64622039a64d9e63ac/cd067/hero.webp 768w,\n/static/c4cf17fff5f67c64622039a64d9e63ac/53334/hero.webp 1024w,\n/static/c4cf17fff5f67c64622039a64d9e63ac/4b075/hero.webp 1280w,\n/static/c4cf17fff5f67c64622039a64d9e63ac/f3ff0/hero.webp 1920w,\n/static/c4cf17fff5f67c64622039a64d9e63ac/4293a/hero.webp 2400w\"\n              sizes=\"(max-width: 1280px) 100vw, 1280px\"\n              type=\"image/webp\"\n            />\n          <source\n            srcset=\"/static/c4cf17fff5f67c64622039a64d9e63ac/d4f27/hero.png 320w,\n/static/c4cf17fff5f67c64622039a64d9e63ac/778aa/hero.png 768w,\n/static/c4cf17fff5f67c64622039a64d9e63ac/658fc/hero.png 1024w,\n/static/c4cf17fff5f67c64622039a64d9e63ac/26c69/hero.png 1280w,\n/static/c4cf17fff5f67c64622039a64d9e63ac/7d442/hero.png 1920w,\n/static/c4cf17fff5f67c64622039a64d9e63ac/00711/hero.png 2400w\"\n            sizes=\"(max-width: 1280px) 100vw, 1280px\"\n            type=\"image/png\"\n          />\n          <img\n            class=\"gatsby-resp-image-image\"\n            src=\"/static/c4cf17fff5f67c64622039a64d9e63ac/26c69/hero.png\"\n            alt=\"hero\"\n            title=\"\"\n            loading=\"lazy\"\n            decoding=\"async\"\n            style=\"width:100%;height:100%;margin:0;vertical-align:middle;position:absolute;top:0;left:0;\"\n          />\n        </picture>\n  </a>\n    </span></p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>TL;DR; Wrap <code class=\"language-text\">generateContentStream</code> from Firebase AI Logic in a streaming <code class=\"language-text\">resource()</code>. Every chunk lands in a signal, the template re-renders on its own in a zoneless app, and the resource's <code class=\"language-text\">abortSignal</code> cancels the old request when the prompt changes. 🎉</p>\n</blockquote>\n<h3>Introduction</h3>\n<p>Waiting several seconds for a full LLM answer and then dropping a wall of text on the screen is the fastest way to make an AI feature feel slow. Streaming fixes most of that perception problem: the first words show up quickly and the rest keep flowing.</p>\n<p>In Angular, 2026 made this pattern much simpler. Angular v21 made zoneless change detection the default for new apps, and Angular v22 marked <code class=\"language-text\">resource()</code>, <code class=\"language-text\">rxResource()</code> and <code class=\"language-text\">httpResource()</code> as stable. That gives us a first-class primitive for \"async data that changes over time\".</p>\n<p>In this article, we'll explore how to connect Gemini's streaming API to a signal, keep it zoneless-friendly, and cancel requests that are no longer relevant.</p>\n<h2>The Problem with \"just await the answer\"</h2>\n<p>The naive version looks like this: call the model, <code class=\"language-text\">await</code> the full response, then set a signal. It works, but:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>the user stares at a spinner for the whole generation time;</li>\n<li>if they change the prompt halfway, the old request keeps running and may overwrite the new answer when it finally resolves;</li>\n<li>teams sometimes \"fix\" the latency by calling the Gemini API straight from the browser with an API key in the bundle. <strong>Never ship a Gemini API key to the browser.</strong></li>\n</ul>\n<p>That last point matters for the choice of SDK. The <code class=\"language-text\">@google/genai</code> SDK is great on a server you control. In the browser, I prefer the Firebase AI Logic client SDK (<code class=\"language-text\">firebase/ai</code>): it is built to be called from web apps, it does not need the Gemini key in your code, and Firebase recommends enforcing App Check as early as possible to protect the API from unauthorized clients.</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Streaming is a UX feature, cancellation is a correctness feature, and key safety is not optional.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<h2>The Solution: a streaming <code class=\"language-text\">resource()</code></h2>\n<p><code class=\"language-text\">resource()</code> accepts a <code class=\"language-text\">stream</code> option instead of <code class=\"language-text\">loader</code>. A streaming loader returns a signal of <code class=\"language-text\">ResourceStreamItem&lt;T></code>, which is either <code class=\"language-text\">{ value }</code> or <code class=\"language-text\">{ error }</code>. It also receives the same <code class=\"language-text\">params</code> and <code class=\"language-text\">abortSignal</code> that a normal loader gets.</p>\n<p>First, the model, created once in a service:</p>\n<div class=\"gatsby-highlight\" data-language=\"typescript\"><pre class=\"language-typescript\"><code class=\"language-typescript\"><span class=\"token comment\">// gemini.service.ts</span>\n<span class=\"token keyword\">import</span> <span class=\"token punctuation\">{</span> Injectable <span class=\"token punctuation\">}</span> <span class=\"token keyword\">from</span> <span class=\"token string\">'@angular/core'</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">;</span>\n<span class=\"token keyword\">import</span> <span class=\"token punctuation\">{</span> initializeApp <span class=\"token punctuation\">}</span> <span class=\"token keyword\">from</span> <span class=\"token string\">'firebase/app'</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">;</span>\n<span class=\"token keyword\">import</span> <span class=\"token punctuation\">{</span> getAI<span class=\"token punctuation\">,</span> getGenerativeModel<span class=\"token punctuation\">,</span> GoogleAIBackend <span class=\"token punctuation\">}</span> <span class=\"token keyword\">from</span> <span class=\"token string\">'firebase/ai'</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">;</span>\n<span class=\"token keyword\">import</span> <span class=\"token punctuation\">{</span> environment <span class=\"token punctuation\">}</span> <span class=\"token keyword\">from</span> <span class=\"token string\">'../environments/environment'</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">;</span>\n\n<span class=\"token decorator\"><span class=\"token at operator\">@</span><span class=\"token function\">Injectable</span></span><span class=\"token punctuation\">(</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">{</span> providedIn<span class=\"token operator\">:</span> <span class=\"token string\">'root'</span> <span class=\"token punctuation\">}</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">)</span>\n<span class=\"token keyword\">export</span> <span class=\"token keyword\">class</span> <span class=\"token class-name\">GeminiService</span> <span class=\"token punctuation\">{</span>\n  <span class=\"token keyword\">private</span> <span class=\"token keyword\">readonly</span> ai <span class=\"token operator\">=</span> <span class=\"token function\">getAI</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">(</span><span class=\"token function\">initializeApp</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">(</span>environment<span class=\"token punctuation\">.</span>firebase<span class=\"token punctuation\">)</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">,</span> <span class=\"token punctuation\">{</span>\n    backend<span class=\"token operator\">:</span> <span class=\"token keyword\">new</span> <span class=\"token class-name\">GoogleAIBackend</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">(</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">)</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">,</span>\n  <span class=\"token punctuation\">}</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">)</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">;</span>\n\n  <span class=\"token comment\">// Check the Firebase AI Logic models page for the current stable name,</span>\n  <span class=\"token comment\">// or drive it from Remote Config so you can change it without a deploy.</span>\n  <span class=\"token keyword\">readonly</span> model <span class=\"token operator\">=</span> <span class=\"token function\">getGenerativeModel</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">(</span><span class=\"token keyword\">this</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">.</span>ai<span class=\"token punctuation\">,</span> <span class=\"token punctuation\">{</span> model<span class=\"token operator\">:</span> <span class=\"token string\">'gemini-3.8-flash'</span> <span class=\"token punctuation\">}</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">)</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">;</span>\n<span class=\"token punctuation\">}</span></code></pre></div>\n<p>Then, the component that turns the prompt into a streamed answer:</p>\n<div class=\"gatsby-highlight\" data-language=\"typescript\"><pre class=\"language-typescript\"><code class=\"language-typescript\"><span class=\"token comment\">// answer.component.ts</span>\n<span class=\"token keyword\">import</span> <span class=\"token punctuation\">{</span> Component<span class=\"token punctuation\">,</span> inject<span class=\"token punctuation\">,</span> resource<span class=\"token punctuation\">,</span> signal<span class=\"token punctuation\">,</span> ResourceStreamItem <span class=\"token punctuation\">}</span> <span class=\"token keyword\">from</span> <span class=\"token string\">'@angular/core'</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">;</span>\n<span class=\"token keyword\">import</span> <span class=\"token punctuation\">{</span> GeminiService <span class=\"token punctuation\">}</span> <span class=\"token keyword\">from</span> <span class=\"token string\">'./gemini.service'</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">;</span>\n\n<span class=\"token decorator\"><span class=\"token at operator\">@</span><span class=\"token function\">Component</span></span><span class=\"token punctuation\">(</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">{</span>\n  selector<span class=\"token operator\">:</span> <span class=\"token string\">'app-answer'</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">,</span>\n  template<span class=\"token operator\">:</span> <span class=\"token template-string\"><span class=\"token template-punctuation string\">`</span><span class=\"token string\">\n    &lt;form (submit)=\"ask($event, q.value)\">\n      &lt;input #q aria-label=\"Your question\" />\n      &lt;button>Ask&lt;/button>\n    &lt;/form>\n\n    @if (answer.error()) {\n      &lt;p role=\"alert\">Something went wrong. Please try again.&lt;/p>\n    }\n    &lt;p aria-live=\"polite\">{{ answer.value() }}&lt;/p>\n    @if (answer.isLoading()) {\n      &lt;span class=\"cursor\" aria-hidden=\"true\">▍&lt;/span>\n    }\n  </span><span class=\"token template-punctuation string\">`</span></span><span class=\"token punctuation\">,</span>\n<span class=\"token punctuation\">}</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">)</span>\n<span class=\"token keyword\">export</span> <span class=\"token keyword\">class</span> <span class=\"token class-name\">AnswerComponent</span> <span class=\"token punctuation\">{</span>\n  <span class=\"token keyword\">private</span> <span class=\"token keyword\">readonly</span> gemini <span class=\"token operator\">=</span> <span class=\"token function\">inject</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">(</span>GeminiService<span class=\"token punctuation\">)</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">;</span>\n  <span class=\"token keyword\">readonly</span> prompt <span class=\"token operator\">=</span> <span class=\"token generic-function\"><span class=\"token function\">signal</span><span class=\"token generic class-name\"><span class=\"token operator\">&lt;</span><span class=\"token builtin\">string</span> <span class=\"token operator\">|</span> <span class=\"token keyword\">undefined</span><span class=\"token operator\">></span></span></span><span class=\"token punctuation\">(</span><span class=\"token keyword\">undefined</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">)</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">;</span>\n\n  <span class=\"token keyword\">readonly</span> answer <span class=\"token operator\">=</span> <span class=\"token function\">resource</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">(</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">{</span>\n    <span class=\"token function-variable function\">params</span><span class=\"token operator\">:</span> <span class=\"token punctuation\">(</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">)</span> <span class=\"token operator\">=></span> <span class=\"token keyword\">this</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">.</span><span class=\"token function\">prompt</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">(</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">)</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">,</span>\n    <span class=\"token function-variable function\">stream</span><span class=\"token operator\">:</span> <span class=\"token keyword\">async</span> <span class=\"token punctuation\">(</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">{</span> params<span class=\"token punctuation\">,</span> abortSignal <span class=\"token punctuation\">}</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">)</span> <span class=\"token operator\">=></span> <span class=\"token punctuation\">{</span>\n      <span class=\"token keyword\">const</span> out <span class=\"token operator\">=</span> <span class=\"token generic-function\"><span class=\"token function\">signal</span><span class=\"token generic class-name\"><span class=\"token operator\">&lt;</span>ResourceStreamItem<span class=\"token operator\">&lt;</span><span class=\"token builtin\">string</span><span class=\"token operator\">>></span></span></span><span class=\"token punctuation\">(</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">{</span> value<span class=\"token operator\">:</span> <span class=\"token string\">''</span> <span class=\"token punctuation\">}</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">)</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">;</span>\n      <span class=\"token keyword\">let</span> text <span class=\"token operator\">=</span> <span class=\"token string\">''</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">;</span>\n\n      <span class=\"token keyword\">try</span> <span class=\"token punctuation\">{</span>\n        <span class=\"token keyword\">const</span> result <span class=\"token operator\">=</span> <span class=\"token keyword\">await</span> <span class=\"token keyword\">this</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">.</span>gemini<span class=\"token punctuation\">.</span>model<span class=\"token punctuation\">.</span><span class=\"token function\">generateContentStream</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">(</span>params<span class=\"token punctuation\">,</span> <span class=\"token punctuation\">{</span>\n          signal<span class=\"token operator\">:</span> abortSignal<span class=\"token punctuation\">,</span>\n        <span class=\"token punctuation\">}</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">)</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">;</span>\n        <span class=\"token punctuation\">(</span><span class=\"token keyword\">async</span> <span class=\"token punctuation\">(</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">)</span> <span class=\"token operator\">=></span> <span class=\"token punctuation\">{</span>\n          <span class=\"token keyword\">try</span> <span class=\"token punctuation\">{</span>\n            <span class=\"token keyword\">for</span> <span class=\"token keyword\">await</span> <span class=\"token punctuation\">(</span><span class=\"token keyword\">const</span> chunk <span class=\"token keyword\">of</span> result<span class=\"token punctuation\">.</span>stream<span class=\"token punctuation\">)</span> <span class=\"token punctuation\">{</span>\n              text <span class=\"token operator\">+=</span> chunk<span class=\"token punctuation\">.</span><span class=\"token function\">text</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">(</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">)</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">;</span>\n              out<span class=\"token punctuation\">.</span><span class=\"token function\">set</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">(</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">{</span> value<span class=\"token operator\">:</span> text <span class=\"token punctuation\">}</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">)</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">;</span>\n            <span class=\"token punctuation\">}</span>\n          <span class=\"token punctuation\">}</span> <span class=\"token keyword\">catch</span> <span class=\"token punctuation\">(</span>e<span class=\"token punctuation\">)</span> <span class=\"token punctuation\">{</span>\n            <span class=\"token keyword\">if</span> <span class=\"token punctuation\">(</span><span class=\"token operator\">!</span>abortSignal<span class=\"token punctuation\">.</span>aborted<span class=\"token punctuation\">)</span> out<span class=\"token punctuation\">.</span><span class=\"token function\">set</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">(</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">{</span> error<span class=\"token operator\">:</span> <span class=\"token function\">toError</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">(</span>e<span class=\"token punctuation\">)</span> <span class=\"token punctuation\">}</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">)</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">;</span>\n          <span class=\"token punctuation\">}</span>\n        <span class=\"token punctuation\">}</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">)</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">(</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">)</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">;</span>\n      <span class=\"token punctuation\">}</span> <span class=\"token keyword\">catch</span> <span class=\"token punctuation\">(</span>e<span class=\"token punctuation\">)</span> <span class=\"token punctuation\">{</span>\n        <span class=\"token keyword\">if</span> <span class=\"token punctuation\">(</span><span class=\"token operator\">!</span>abortSignal<span class=\"token punctuation\">.</span>aborted<span class=\"token punctuation\">)</span> out<span class=\"token punctuation\">.</span><span class=\"token function\">set</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">(</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">{</span> error<span class=\"token operator\">:</span> <span class=\"token function\">toError</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">(</span>e<span class=\"token punctuation\">)</span> <span class=\"token punctuation\">}</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">)</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">;</span>\n      <span class=\"token punctuation\">}</span>\n\n      <span class=\"token keyword\">return</span> out<span class=\"token punctuation\">;</span>\n    <span class=\"token punctuation\">}</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">,</span>\n  <span class=\"token punctuation\">}</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">)</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">;</span>\n\n  <span class=\"token function\">ask</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">(</span>event<span class=\"token operator\">:</span> Event<span class=\"token punctuation\">,</span> value<span class=\"token operator\">:</span> <span class=\"token builtin\">string</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">)</span> <span class=\"token punctuation\">{</span>\n    event<span class=\"token punctuation\">.</span><span class=\"token function\">preventDefault</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">(</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">)</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">;</span>\n    <span class=\"token keyword\">this</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">.</span>prompt<span class=\"token punctuation\">.</span><span class=\"token function\">set</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">(</span>value<span class=\"token punctuation\">.</span><span class=\"token function\">trim</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">(</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">)</span> <span class=\"token operator\">||</span> <span class=\"token keyword\">undefined</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">)</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">;</span>\n  <span class=\"token punctuation\">}</span>\n<span class=\"token punctuation\">}</span>\n\n<span class=\"token keyword\">function</span> <span class=\"token function\">toError</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">(</span>e<span class=\"token operator\">:</span> <span class=\"token builtin\">unknown</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">)</span><span class=\"token operator\">:</span> Error <span class=\"token punctuation\">{</span>\n  <span class=\"token keyword\">return</span> e <span class=\"token keyword\">instanceof</span> <span class=\"token class-name\">Error</span> <span class=\"token operator\">?</span> e <span class=\"token operator\">:</span> <span class=\"token keyword\">new</span> <span class=\"token class-name\">Error</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">(</span><span class=\"token function\">String</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">(</span>e<span class=\"token punctuation\">)</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">)</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">;</span>\n<span class=\"token punctuation\">}</span></code></pre></div>\n<p>As you can see, there is no <code class=\"language-text\">NgZone</code>, no <code class=\"language-text\">ChangeDetectorRef</code> and no <code class=\"language-text\">async</code> pipe. Let's go through the pieces that make it work.</p>\n<h4>1. Signals drive rendering, so zoneless just works</h4>\n<p>Each <code class=\"language-text\">out.set(...)</code> writes to a signal the template reads through <code class=\"language-text\">answer.value()</code>. In a zoneless app, that signal write is what schedules change detection, so nothing depends on Zone.js patching the <code class=\"language-text\">for await</code> loop. With <code class=\"language-text\">OnPush</code> now the default for components in Angular v22, this is exactly the shape Angular expects.</p>\n<h4>2. <code class=\"language-text\">params</code> returning <code class=\"language-text\">undefined</code> keeps the resource idle</h4>\n<p>Before the user asks anything, <code class=\"language-text\">prompt()</code> is <code class=\"language-text\">undefined</code>, the stream never runs and the status stays <code class=\"language-text\">'idle'</code>. No accidental empty request on first render.</p>\n<h4>3. Cancellation comes for free</h4>\n<p>When <code class=\"language-text\">prompt</code> changes while a stream is still running, the resource aborts the previous operation through <code class=\"language-text\">abortSignal</code>. Passing it to <code class=\"language-text\">generateContentStream</code> as <code class=\"language-text\">{ signal: abortSignal }</code> (a <code class=\"language-text\">SingleRequestOptions</code> field in <code class=\"language-text\">firebase/ai</code>) attempts to cancel the underlying HTTP request. The old answer never overwrites the new one.</p>\n<p>Keep in mind one detail from the Firebase reference: aborting does not cancel the request in the backend, so billing still applies. Cancellation protects your UI, not your quota. Debounce or rate-limit the input if users can fire many prompts quickly.</p>\n<h4>4. Errors are values, not crashes</h4>\n<p>The stream reports failures as <code class=\"language-text\">{ error }</code>, so <code class=\"language-text\">answer.error()</code> and <code class=\"language-text\">answer.status()</code> reflect them. I check <code class=\"language-text\">abortSignal.aborted</code> first, so an intentional cancellation is not shown as a failure.</p>\n<h2>What about <code class=\"language-text\">rxResource</code> or <code class=\"language-text\">@google/genai</code>?</h2>\n<p>If your app already has an RxJS pipeline (for example, a backend that sends Server-Sent Events), <code class=\"language-text\">rxResource()</code> from <code class=\"language-text\">@angular/core/rxjs-interop</code> takes a <code class=\"language-text\">stream</code> function that returns an <code class=\"language-text\">Observable</code>, and the same ideas apply.</p>\n<p>If you need server-only features or want to keep prompts private, put <code class=\"language-text\">@google/genai</code> behind your own endpoint, stream the response with SSE, and point the resource at that endpoint. The browser side stays the same: chunks in, signal out, abort on change.</p>\n<h2>Conclusion</h2>\n<p>Streaming plus signals is one of those combinations that feels obvious once you see it. The resource owns the lifecycle, the signal owns the rendering, and the <code class=\"language-text\">abortSignal</code> owns correctness. If you want to make the waiting part feel even better, the next posts in this series cover <a href=\"/posts/skeleton-loaders-for-llm-latency-ngx-skeleton-loader-for-streaming-uis/\">skeleton loaders for streaming UIs</a> and <a href=\"/posts/feature-flagging-gemini-features-in-angular-with-ngx-feature-toggle/\">feature flagging Gemini features</a>. For the on-device side of Firebase AI Logic, check <a href=\"/posts/hybrid-inference-with-firebase-ai-logic-on-device-first-cloud-fallback/\">hybrid inference with Firebase AI Logic</a>.</p>\n<h2>References</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><a href=\"https://angular.dev/guide/signals/resource\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow noopener noreferrer\">Angular: Async reactivity with resources</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"https://angular.dev/guide/zoneless\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow noopener noreferrer\">Angular: Zoneless</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"https://firebase.google.com/docs/ai-logic/stream-responses\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow noopener noreferrer\">Firebase AI Logic: Stream responses</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"https://firebase.google.com/docs/ai-logic/generate-text\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow noopener noreferrer\">Firebase AI Logic: Generate text</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"https://firebase.google.com/docs/ai-logic/models\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow noopener noreferrer\">Firebase AI Logic: Supported models</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"https://firebase.google.com/docs/reference/js/ai.singlerequestoptions\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow noopener noreferrer\">Firebase JS reference: <code class=\"language-text\">SingleRequestOptions</code></a></li>\n<li><a href=\"https://firebase.google.com/docs/reference/js/ai.generativemodel\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow noopener noreferrer\">Firebase JS reference: <code class=\"language-text\">GenerativeModel.generateContentStream</code></a></li>\n</ul>\n<h3>That’s all for now</h3>\n<p>Stream the words, keep the key on the server side of the trust boundary, and let the resource handle cancellation for you.</p>\n<p>I hope you enjoyed this reading as much as I enjoyed writing it. Thank you so much for reading until the end and see you soon!</p>\n<p>🚀🚀🚀🚀🚀🚀</p>\n<hr />\n<h3>Cya 👋</h3>","frontmatter":{"date":"November 23, 2026","path":"/posts/streaming-gemini-responses-into-angular-signals/","title":"Streaming Gemini responses into Angular signals — resource(), zoneless and cancellation","tags":["angular","ai","gemini","frontend","performance","web"],"status":"active"},"timeToRead":5}},"pageContext":{"postPath":"/posts/streaming-gemini-responses-into-angular-signals/"}},"staticQueryHashes":["1271460761","63159454"],"slicesMap":{}}